{"comments":[{"id":"2a0b9033-c120-4c59-ba02-235b7b8eb5c1","body":"Recovery coordinator engineering disposition: the historical block is exclusive cross-file ownership, not a changed behavioral acceptance choice. One isolated semantic writer is assigned the reconciler types/actual graph, native pre-persist AgentRunner/AgentService seam, Ralph verdict production/state/reporting and production constructor wiring as one review unit. This authorizes coherent wiring under the existing Check (the widened-owner option), not a partial self-asserting stage table or a founder behavioral ruling. 812's actual fresh structured-output dispatch and813's produced retained verdict channel belong to this same owner.

Current canonical593fdc1 has no semantic reconciler. Source inspection confirms a node after Ralph execute would be too late because stream_workflow already invokes ChangePersister.persist. The required gate must run while the native writer workspace remains owned, before the harness creates/pushes or replays a commit, and all actual native writer stages must route through it. Authored-path compatibility remains required.

An additional enforcement limit is explicit: a post-stream gate cannot prevent an agent that already has shell access from making its own local commit. The native contract will snapshot/refuse changed HEAD before harness persistence and prevent harness publication; it must not be described as preventing every arbitrary agent-side action. The worker is checking the resolved SDK's supported capability controls and preserving this limit if they cannot establish stronger prevention. No source acceptance or branch protection override follows from this assignment; KOD814's separate native artifact behavior fork remains held.","attachments":[],"createdAt":"2026-09-12T15:04:16.121Z","updatedAt":"2026-09-12T15:04:16.085Z","parentId":null,"resolvedAt":null,"quotedText":null,"author":{"id":"998f68f9-58c0-4c31-bdc8-2b9d8da803a2","name":"Goofy"},"onBehalfOf":null}],"hasNextPage":false}
